{"v":1,"accession":"PRJNA326216","title":"Wilanow Palace velvet silk wall decorations metagenome","description":"Nowadays, the need to determine the microbial communities inhabiting particular museum environmentsit is widely understood. The diversity of microorganisms residing on an art object, their quantity and metabolic potential are of the great importance for its conservation and future preservation. The aim of this study was to assess the diversity of microbial populations present on historical silk velvet decorations surfaces potentially contributing to the biodegradation of silk proteins.","center":"Institute of Biochemistry and Biophysics Polish Academy of Sciences","data_type":"Metagenome","submission_date":"2016/06/20 00:00","sample_cols":["accession","title","tier","context","collection_date","collection_year","country","region","place_id","place","location_status","lat","lon","submitted_location","isolation_source","env_broad_scale","env_local_scale","env_medium","eligibility_reason"],"samples":[["SAMN05289730","Velvet decorations from king’s antechamber, disinfected, vacuumed","confirmed_urban","built_environment","2008-06-20",2008,"PL","Mazovia",756135,"Warsaw","verified",52.1652,21.0884,"Poland: Warsaw",null,"urban biome","building","anthropogenic environmental material","explicit urban setting at sample level"],["SAMN05289731","Velvet decorations from king’s antechamber, disinfected, vacuumed","confirmed_urban","built_environment","2008-06-20",2008,"PL","Mazovia",756135,"Warsaw","verified",52.1652,21.0884,"Poland: Warsaw",null,"urban biome","building","anthropogenic environmental material","explicit urban setting at sample level"],["SAMN05289732","Velvet decorations from queen’s antechamber, disinfected, vacuumed","confirmed_urban","built_environment","2008-06-20",2008,"PL","Mazovia",756135,"Warsaw","verified",52.1652,21.0884,"Poland: Warsaw",null,"urban biome","building","anthropogenic environmental material","explicit urban setting at sample level